<h2 id="brauer-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="073X">11.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
A reference is the lectures by Serre in the Seminaire Cartan, see <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Serre-Cartan">Serre-Cartan</a>]</span>. Serre in turn refers to <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Deuring">Deuring</a>]</span> and <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/ANT">ANT</a>]</span>. We changed some of the proofs, in particular we used a fun argument of Rieffel to prove Wedderburn's theorem. Very likely this change is not an improvement and we strongly encourage the reader to read the original exposition by Serre. 
</p>
